#. type: Title #
#: content/tags/2026-collab/_index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Disaster Preparedness, Response and Relief"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/tags/2026-collab/_index.en.md
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The works below are a selection of illustrations created for the 2025 "
#| "Solarpunk Art Collab ran by the Story Seed Library and [Andrewism]"
#| "(https://www.youtube.com/@Andrewism/)."
msgid ""
"The works below are a selection of illustrations created for the 2026 "
"Solarpunk Art Collab ran by the Story Seed Library and [Andrewism](https://"
"www.youtube.com/@Andrewism/)."
msgstr ""
"Роботи нижче були створені в рамках проєкту Художницький колаб 2025, який "
"провели люди з Бібліотеки Саджанців Історій та [Andrewism](https://"
"www.youtube.com/@Andrewism/)."

#. type: Plain text
#: content/tags/2026-collab/_index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> Even in the most optimistic scenarios of carbon neutrality, the XXI century will be full of climate disasters our civilization, culture and infrastructure are not prepared for. Let's step away from clean, utopian Solarpunk worlds and roll our sleeves to face the consequences of our past.\n"
">\n"
"> How can a better Solarpunk world react to the coming disasters? How will our daily lives change? What new or repurposed infrastructure will keep us safe? What new traditions will we need to guide us? What stories will we tell ourselves to make sense of the world that has changed so much?\n"
">\n"
"> Let's imagine more than just the rising waters: the droughts and fires, the sudden floods and pandemics, loss of infrastructure and supply chains we take for granted.\n"
">\n"
"> Finally, for the Disaster Relief, how can we step away from our colonial habits and imagine giving the survivors agency instead of handouts? How can we empower communities to rebuild after a catastrophe, find solace in each other and grieve those lost?\n"
msgstr ""

